# The shares of executable functions and of their lines that the verus
# check holds main to (the kit counter (verus-count) with --floor;
# verus/README.md, "Coverage"):
# the counter's `shipped` row, every function under src/ but test code,
# rounded down to a tenth of a percent.
#
# The four figure names are the ones the kit's counter reads.
# `functions` and `lines` are the verified share: Verus checks them.
# `checked-functions` and `checked-lines` add the trusted functions Kani
# discharges (with the generated-ledger back end, the seams the ledger
# marks discharged, verus/SEAMS.md, "Status"), which hold on the bounded
# inputs their records under verus/seams/ name.
#
# New executable code comes with its proofs (CONTRIBUTING.md), so a change
# keeps each share at or above these figures. The check passes a share
# above its figure and names the figure to record. The figures, and the
# README badge that shows them, rise in a pull request of their own, to
# the figures the check names, never in the pull request that earns them,
# so that pull requests landing in parallel do not conflict here. The one
# exception is the port's first proof pull request, which may raise every
# figure from 0.0 in the same pull request, whether it brings the counter
# or the counter landed earlier with every figure at 0.0.
#
# README.md's Verus badge gives `functions` and `lines` as written here
# (verus/count.toml's `[badge]`), and the check fails when it does not, so
# the change that moves either figure replaces the badge line with the one
# `verus-count --badge .` prints.
#
# The base revision is the one Checks sets: the pull request's base on a
# pull request, and on main the start of the push the run covers, main
# before its first merge (.chainguard/ci/verus.yaml). A figure
# set below the base revision's fails unless a
# `lowered FIGURE P REASON` line here, new in that change, names that
# figure and value.
#
# A `lowered` line is the last resort: close the gap by verifying more
# code first. Its REASON names exactly what became trusted or outside, and
# the counts before and after (`N of M shipped functions verified, P%,
# against main's SHA at N' of M'`).

# challoc: one crate at the root, which ships though its Cargo.toml says
# `publish = false` (verus/count.toml's `ships`). The checked figures were
# `combined-functions` and `combined-lines` before they took the kit's
# names (verus/count.toml's `renamed_from`, so a base revision's copy
# still compares), and mean the same: verified, plus the trusted functions
# whose seam the ledger marks discharged, by Kani or Isla, on premises
# included. challoc keeps its Kani and Isla records under verus/kani/ and
# verus/isla/, which the ledger entries name, not under verus/seams/. The
# rule the header cites from CONTRIBUTING.md is verus/README.md's
# ("Coverage").
functions 86.6
lines 94.5
checked-functions 91.7
checked-lines 96.7
